    "doc": "E-026 arm: stencil:17 RING r=222 km (centre + SIXTEEN points), seed 0. Chris: 'I am not sure I trust the ridges, linear is not enough -- try our stage 2 transformer on the ring of 8 vs the ring of 16.' Paired against e023r222 (same radius, same recipe, same seeds, EIGHT points, corridor AUC 0.6043) and e017 (no neighbours, 0.5837); both already trained and already rolled by the same evaluator behind the same gate, so no new controls are needed. The width question is where the ridge and E-022 predict OPPOSITE things about this model: the ridge says 16 points buy what 8 buy (+0.0134 vs +0.0140), E-022 says the real model pays for width (9 and 13 touching neighbours came out 6.3 and 8.1 seed sd worse than none, with zero-weight equivalence proving it could have ignored them). Falsifier: corridor AUC above ~0.619. Entry: ml/EXPERIMENTS.md E-026.",
